-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OilAndGasPropertyFullCostMethodDepletion" scale="3" id="Tc_gVJKx6tr5kyGASg2GhCSuw_4_3">151,446</ix:nonFraction>)</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:3.14%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.98%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:16.16%;background:#cceeff;border-bottom:1px solid #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> (<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_A6l7VhAU8UabbTuqZPYlYQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OilAndGasPropertyFullCostMethodDepletion" scale="3" id="Tc_F8bGy_Q6X0udv8rZyBjqsg_4_6">130,248</ix:nonFraction>)</p></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:57.41%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 6pt;">Oil and natural gas properties, net</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:3.12%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 6pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;margin-left:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.98%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:16.18%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_Y2rxENVYSUG0GoqBco7ecg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasFullCostMethodPropertyAndEquipment" scale="3" id="Tc_21cnu4lYQE-WdcT856E3qg_5_3">146,967</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:3.14%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:9pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.98%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;">$</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:16.16%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_A6l7VhAU8UabbTuqZPYlYQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasFullCostMethodPropertyAndEquipment" scale="3" id="Tc_IH8R6RmAdUmiUVDlTpd7dw_5_6">142,248</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">58</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">EVOLUTION PETROLEUM CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_u6RQFFD1xEqCKx7wGgQq0g_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company uses the full cost method of accounting for its investments in oil and natural gas properties. All costs of acquisition, exploration, and development of oil and natural gas reserves are capitalized as the cost of oil and natural gas properties when incurred. To the extent capitalized costs of evaluated oil and natural gas properties, net of accumulated depletion, exceed the discounted future net revenues of proved oil and natural gas reserves, net of deferred taxes, such excess capitalized costs would be charged to expense as a write-down of oil and natural gas properties.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Additionally, the Company assesses all properties classified as unproved property on a quarterly basis for possible impairment. The Company assesses properties on an individual basis or as a group, if properties are individually insignificant. The assessment includes consideration of the following factors, among others: intent to drill; remaining lease term; geological and geophysical evaluations; drilling results and activity; the assignment of proved reserves; and the economic viability of development if proved reserves are assigned. During any period in which these factors indicate impairment, the cumulative drilling costs incurred to date for such property and all or a portion of the associated leasehold costs are transferred to the full cost pool and are then subject to depletion and the full cost ceiling test limitation.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June 30, 2026 and 2025, all oil and natural gas property costs were subject to amortization. Depletion on oil and natural gas properties was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depletion" scale="6" id="Narr_2kEfYua6X0KTrRBHBeRfpg">21.2</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_THEX2ddrdkiphXD1ngVTwA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Depletion" scale="6" id="Narr_UYs_9jaY70ChPBvleADoZg">20.4</ix:nonFraction> million for the&#160;years ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025, respectively. During the&#160;years ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025, the Company incurred development capital expenditures of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CapitalExpendituresIncurredButNotYetPaid" scale="6" id="Narr_bn9uKRyRm023E5rzPO7oSA">5.5</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_THEX2ddrdkiphXD1ngVTwA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CapitalExpendituresIncurredButNotYetPaid" scale="6" id="Narr_Q7iVgYwh3kKpJ4fw5i8Meg">13.2</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">At June&#160;30,&#160;2026, the ceiling test value of the Company&#8217;s reserves was calculated based on the first-day-of-the-month average for the 12-months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 of the West Texas Intermediate (&#8220;WTI&#8221;) crude oil spot price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_bbl_2uTFxettp0-uug0GGQvoHw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_CrudeOilMember_yR4c7C3xAEeA7t2BQUftWQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasPricesFirstDayAverageOfTwelveMonthsOfWestTexasIntermediateSpotMarketPriceForCeilingTest" scale="0" id="Narr_r5ARu1zVhUyxPkezeZZvPg">72.93</ix:nonFraction> per barrel and Henry Hub natural gas spot price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_MMBTU_Z1NAgPlFCkirdl89JHqsRQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_NaturalGasPerThousandCubicFeetMember_er_qYaO1PEux8Xg1TjUURw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasPricesFirstDayAverageOfTwelveMonthsOfHenryHubPriceForCeilingTest" scale="0" id="Narr_d6g7stMbtEqOlulUDetFtQ">3.62</ix:nonFraction> per MMBtu, adjusted by market differentials by field. The net price per barrel of NGLs was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_bbl_2uTFxettp0-uug0GGQvoHw" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_NaturalGasPerThousandCubicFeetMember_jWI7046LAk-lMMRm-qnAvw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="srt:ConsolidatedOilAndGasProductionCostsPerUnitOfProduction" scale="0" id="Narr_gZ_6dgpBmkWhGhxTyDpgvw">27.50</ix:nonFraction>, which was based on historical differentials to WTI as NGLs do not have any single comparable reference index price. Using these prices, at June&#160;30,&#160;2026 the cost center ceiling was higher than the capitalized costs of oil and natural gas properties, subject to amortization, and, as a result, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" decimals="-5" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfOilAndGasProperties" scale="6" id="Narr_1yJQ3T-chEC8NEXqhLpZ6Q">no</ix:nonFraction> write-down was applicable.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">At June&#160;30,&#160;2025, the ceiling test value of the Company&#8217;s reserves was calculated based on the first-day-of-the-month average for the 12-months ended June&#160;30,&#160;2025 of the WTI crude oil spot price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_bbl_2uTFxettp0-uug0GGQvoHw" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_CrudeOilMember_NA_En49p102AefTWEagCjw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasPricesFirstDayAverageOfTwelveMonthsOfWestTexasIntermediateSpotMarketPriceForCeilingTest" scale="0" id="Narr_EcYJ4Ffhl0CVu9PArQMzmQ">71.20</ix:nonFraction> per barrel and Henry Hub natural gas spot price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_MMBTU_Z1NAgPlFCkirdl89JHqsRQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_NaturalGasPerThousandCubicFeetMember_9kM1z7h58UCEJ6onfWZlQg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:OilAndGasPricesFirstDayAverageOfTwelveMonthsOfHenryHubPriceForCeilingTest" scale="0" id="Narr_XUI-NQM1QEu004YDt4G2_w">2.87</ix:nonFraction> per MMBtu, adjusted by market differentials by field. The net price per barrel of NGLs was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_bbl_2uTFxettp0-uug0GGQvoHw" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_NaturalGasPerThousandCubicFeetMember_AstESrdmbECoKGhwwxW_ug" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="srt:ConsolidatedOilAndGasProductionCostsPerUnitOfProduction" scale="0" id="Narr_hsw-Py5dm0ajBRo1bnDwgw">25.24</ix:nonFraction>, which was based on historical differentials to WTI as NGLs do not have any single comparable reference index price. Using these prices, at June&#160;30,&#160;2025 the cost center ceiling was higher than the capitalized costs of oil and natural gas properties, subject to amortization, and, as a result, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2024_To_6_30_2025_THEX2ddrdkiphXD1ngVTwA" decimals="-5" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:ImpairmentOfOilAndGasProperties" scale="6" id="Narr_QVXYFNPWEUiF8qGJ7tLtiA">no</ix:nonFraction> write-down was applicable. </p></ix:continuation><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" name="us-gaap:DebtDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_R6AS_MWvqE-6KGwsnXEBEg" continuedAt="Tb_R6AS_MWvqE-6KGwsnXEBEg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Note&#160;5. Senior Secured Credit Facility</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On April&#160;11, 2016, the Company entered into a senior secured reserve-based credit facility with MidFirst Bank in an amount up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_11_2016_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_7_w0LKlC-Em9tyFxYKyt2w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_vObVO7T1s0iG8q4rmy6rCw">50.0</ix:nonFraction> million. On June 30, 2025, the Company entered into a syndicated amended and restated senior secured reserve-based credit facility (the &#8220;Senior Secured Credit Facility&#8221;) with MidFirst Bank, as administrative agent for the lenders party, thereto, in an amount up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityMaximumBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_DOjNxPXgw0OBZFIB_hBQVg">200.0</ix:nonFraction> million with an initial borrowing base of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:LineOfCreditFacilityInitialBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_ubeiW0NgN0SXKv8S3WKRTg">65.0</ix:nonFraction> million, maturing on June 30, 2028. As of June 30, 2026, the borrowing base was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityCurrentBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_q5o7aMbepkWY6LcPfpt99Q">65.0</ix:nonFraction> million. The borrowing base will be redetermined semiannually, with the lenders and the Company each having the right to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_agreement_AZdyRPgtdkCCxkzRwd2XtQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="epm:CreditFacilityNumberOfRightsToInterimUnscheduledRedeterminations" scale="0" id="Narr_BJIa12TJxEi1IDERGweWoA">one</ix:nonFraction> interim unscheduled redetermination between any two consecutive semi-annual redeterminations. The borrowing base takes into account the estimated value of the Company&#8217;s oil and natural gas properties, proved reserves, total indebtedness, and other relevant factors consistent with customary oil and natural gas lending criteria. The Senior Secured Credit Facility carries a commitment fee of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_xkHoaEiz_Eih8qZ2fpKb6A" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityCommitmentFeePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_btzmeZ-5T0CBOuT_LKuOqA">0.25</ix:nonFraction>% per annum on the undrawn portion of the borrowing base. Any borrowings under the Senior Secured Credit Facility will bear interest, at the Company&#8217;s option, at either (i) the Secured Overnight Financing Rate (&#8220;SOFR&#8221;), subject to a minimum SOFR of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrOvernightIndexSwapRateMember_WWFcUhQQzE2tAAhJR-3htw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_zgCba8Foh0GiaJusA3T94g">3.25</ix:nonFraction>%, plus a credit spread adjustment of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_SecuredOvernightFinancingRateSofrOvernightIndexSwapRateMember_dl8MLFVqM0uG36sLpzk7dQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:CreditSpreadAdjustment" scale="-2" id="Narr_vDXKEaUx002p1zsoPkTaJA">0.05</ix:nonFraction>%, or (ii) the Prime Rate, as defined under the Senior Secured Credit Facility, plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_VariableRateAxis_us-gaap_PrimeRateMember_HRsiYWMLw0OinOmErhMGHQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_OqXk5LVjfku4uDRo6ccvYw">1.00</ix:nonFraction>%, plus, in either case of (i) or (ii), an applicable margin of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_xkHoaEiz_Eih8qZ2fpKb6A" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-2" id="Narr_UcD92dw_6ECQsT5_jg9naA">2.75</ix:nonFraction>%.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">59</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">EVOLUTION PETROLEUM CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_R6AS_MWvqE-6KGwsnXEBEg_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_R6AS_MWvqE-6KGwsnXEBEg_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company may elect, at its option, to prepay any borrowings outstanding under the Senior Secured Credit Facility without premium or penalty. Amounts outstanding under the Senior Secured Credit Facility are guaranteed by the Company&#8217;s direct and indirect subsidiaries and secured by a security interest in substantially all of the properties of the Company and its subsidiaries. Borrowings under the Senior Secured Credit Facility may be used for the acquisition and for the drilling and development of oil and natural gas properties, investments in cash flow generating properties complimentary to the production of oil and natural gas, and for letters of credit or other general corporate purposes.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Senior Secured Credit Facility contains certain events of default, including non-payment; breaches of representation and warranties; non-compliance with covenants; cross-defaults to material indebtedness; voluntary or involuntary bankruptcy; judgments and change in control. The Senior Secured Credit Facility also contains financial covenants including a requirement that the Company maintain, as of the last day of each fiscal quarter, (i)&#160;a maximum total leverage ratio of not more than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_4_11_2016_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_7_w0LKlC-Em9tyFxYKyt2w" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtCovenantMaximumTotalLeverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_JEnu9sONmkecIz1nMxGf5A">3.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00, (ii)&#160;a current ratio of not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_4_11_2016_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_7_w0LKlC-Em9tyFxYKyt2w" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumCurrentRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_rbj1FLTOAky271MllGsZyw">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00, and (iii)&#160;a consolidated tangible net worth of not less than $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_11_2016_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_7_w0LKlC-Em9tyFxYKyt2w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:LineOfCreditFacilityCovenantComplianceMinimumConsolidatedTangibleNetWorth" scale="6" id="Narr_QW5yR_rs5UWJVG9PkAo_JQ">40.0</ix:nonFraction> million, each as defined in the Senior Secured Credit Facility. <span style="background:#ffffff;">In addition, the Senior Secured Credit Facility contains hedging requirements that apply when&#160;utilization is greater than </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="Duration_6_30_2025_To_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_xkHoaEiz_Eih8qZ2fpKb6A" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtInstrumentHedgingRequirementsUtilizationPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_98sBojgNqEOl4LKBqbEOLA">25</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> of (x) the Margined Collateral Value, as defined under the Senior Secured Credit Facility, at any time when the leverage ratio is less than </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtInstrumentLeverageRatioTriggerForHedging" scale="0" id="Narr_mAclLiwCKE6NZCtbsF2UAA">2.25</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> to 1.00, or (y) the borrowing base, at any time when the leverage ratio is greater than or equal to </span><span style="background:#ffffff;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtInstrumentLeverageRatioTriggerForHedging" scale="0" id="Narr_eBfMdI8ZKEedhREX7FDOUA">2.25</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="background:#ffffff;"> to 1.00.</span> As of June&#160;30,&#160;2026, the Company had $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCredit" scale="6" id="Narr_Vqa-UUztl06krnscrzMDPQ">56.5</ix:nonFraction> million borrowings outstanding and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LettersOfCreditOutstandingAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_STqAce6Kn0mfw2OhPQckig">0.8</ix:nonFraction> million in letters of credit outstanding under its Senior Secured Credit Facility, resulting in $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityRemainingBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr__66_i-jrSk-MBoDWeEUyXQ">7.7</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million of available borrowing capacity. For the years ended June 30, 2025 and 2024, the weighted average interest rate on borrowings under the Senior Secured Credit Facility was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_6dHCqLalRkGg0P1TotJDcw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtWeightedAverageInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_jUH1Kd2eQEefVJOe0AqFqw">6.69</ix:nonFraction>% and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_dyZD2PMnSUSrs42nKFuzIA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtWeightedAverageInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_NFxzLa_lkE6hQMUQSA3U3g">7.48</ix:nonFraction>%<span style="white-space:pre-wrap;">, respectively.  </span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On November 28, 2025, the Company entered into a letter agreement with MidFirst Bank pursuant to which Margined Collateral Value, as defined under the Senior Secured Credit Facility, was modified to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_11_28_2025_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_lQz2HF8-pkCA5sUDLxABBA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCollateralAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_1JCtQ1pZEkib7VUBWJWgZg">65.0</ix:nonFraction> million. In addition, it granted the Company additional time to enter into further commodity hedges to meet the hedging requirements under the Senior Secured Credit Facility. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On August 29, 2025, the Company entered into the first amendment of its Senior Secured Credit Facility with MidFirst Bank, pursuant to which it was determined for purposes of the hedge covenant that total crude oil and natural gas volumes from proved developed producing reserves will be combined on a barrels of oil equivalent basis to determine compliance with the required hedging covenant.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On March 7, 2025, the Company entered into a letter agreement with MidFirst Bank, which allows for the option to hedge <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_3_7_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_NaturalGasPerThousandCubicFeetMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_LineOfCreditMember_svaoajnP3UO9KP1eb82e7Q" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:PercentageOfOptionForProductionHedge" scale="-2" id="Narr_dXYeMimB4ES2M25G_XNZuQ">72</ix:nonFraction>% of expected natural gas production rather than hedging <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_3_7_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_CrudeOilMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_LineOfCreditMember__QQi61Z3eE2XQgnqR0gRhQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:PercentageOfProductionHedged" scale="-2" id="Narr__xk4--wbXUO5KNUHwo0wsg">25</ix:nonFraction>% of expected crude oil production in each month of the calendar year ending December, 31, 2026, as long as the Company remains in the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_MNvIlwZMlEOOc9YY0CHEUg" contextRef="As_Of_3_7_2025_srt_EnergyAxis_srt_CrudeOilAndNGLPerBarrelMember_us-gaap_CreditFacilityAxis_us-gaap_RevolvingCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_LineOfCreditMember_NG5s7TMUZkCUOld62_QUOQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:PercentageOfBorrowingBaseToMarginedCollateralValue" scale="-2" id="Narr_YEeplussF0aSPFV7gh_sCg">25</ix:nonFraction>%<span style="white-space:pre-wrap;"> required hedging tier.  See Note 7, </span><i style="font-style:italic;">&#8220;Derivatives,&#8221;</i> for a listing of all crude oil and natural gas derivative contracts the Company has entered into.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June&#160;30,&#160;2026, the Company was in compliance with all covenants under the Senior Secured Credit Facility</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company capitalizes certain direct costs associated with its Senior Secured Credit Facility and amortizes these costs over the life of the facility. For the year ended June 30, 2026, the Company amortized $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_kl5SKZSqjUatTWV1DgFjsA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AmortizationOfFinancingCosts" scale="6" id="Narr_ZDTuGDGtEEGjXSN8-B3Lvg">0.2</ix:nonFraction> million and capitalized $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="epm:DebtIssuanceCostsCapitalized" scale="6" id="Narr_i06rWaY-VUakfDYN-xydnQ">0.1</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million of debt issuance costs in conjunction with amending and restating the Senior Secured Credit Facility. The debt issuance costs are presented in&#160;&#8220;<i style="font-style:italic;">Other Assets, net</i>&#8221; on the consolidated balance sheets<span style="font-family:'Times';background:#ffffff;">.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Subsequent to fiscal year end, on August 20, 2026, the Company entered into a letter agreement with MidFirst Bank pursuant to which the borrowing base on its Senior Secured Credit Facility was temporarily increased from $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_bTK9Rm_fYEe45_9-k2fF5w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityCurrentBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_rOLx1VdR8USv-E0GMSamTg">65.0</ix:nonFraction> million to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_8_20_2026_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_epm_SeniorSecuredReserveBasedCreditFacilityMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_gcC4xiKLdU6ihq0LToHv1w" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LineOfCreditFacilityCurrentBorrowingCapacity" scale="6" id="Narr_mYY2Ls6F9kugmUUQV9gjIA">73.0</ix:nonFraction> million from August 20, 2026 until October 20, 2026, unless redetermined in accordance with the terms of the credit agreement. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">60</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">EVOLUTION PETROLEUM CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_R6AS_MWvqE-6KGwsnXEBEg_cont2"></ix:continuation><a id="_9edb2247_d950_4a63_a596_4f2f6209bf01"></a><a id="Tc_gZyWsfysK0KCrGHiJorXlg_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_f08s-IdW30GGUJE97zNxkA_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_G2xmHHbPtECB9nk0RhgbbA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_oYptIUTpUkyrmRGHw00dMQ_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_UBgwStfGsEyGQPktCJIVRw_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_xTl_pKBysEalVd-WsCC8eA_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_OFUe313sakWtAUlZCwMqeQ_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_7hAp1p9zkE2J837rl4Jxfw_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_V1f-OQKpjkiLiGLYDLMFag_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_4HpSsDLVuEGzA8vXuyKQdg_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_WFnsVNkTmk66PxqMLJjcOQ_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_qSGEiKWCGUGv9FczUvTMtQ_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_-XsEHW8YlECvwthGhmQCKA_10_0"></a><a id="Tc_6Hor2fzFgEOrEmFCIuL9CA_10_2"></a><a id="Tc_Rurok0A_gU-VxzAgQhmaYA_10_5"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_TmZhIgXhokK_wOccA3ta9A" continuedAt="Tb_TmZhIgXhokK_wOccA3ta9A_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Note&#160;6. Income Taxes</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company files&#160;a consolidated federal income tax return in the United States and various combined and separate filings in several state and local jurisdictions in a timely manner.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">There were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_A6l7VhAU8UabbTuqZPYlYQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:UnrecognizedTaxBenefits" scale="0" id="Narr_MNbUseY1CES1bX3llZoFxQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_Y2rxENVYSUG0GoqBco7ecg" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:UnrecognizedTaxBenefits" scale="0" id="Narr_iHO0WeN5zE26zJZktJl8LA">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> unrecognized tax benefits, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2025_A6l7VhAU8UabbTuqZPYlYQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:UnrecognizedTaxBenefitsIncomeTaxPenaltiesAndInterestAccrued" scale="0" id="Narr_pc4Yz4ylmEiaTj0CKFFFwg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_gDp5XCeWnEippY-t1_RnwQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_Y2rxENVYSUG0GoqBco7ecg" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:UnrecognizedTaxBenefitsIncomeTaxPenaltiesAndInterestAccrued" scale="0" id="Narr_zIzyVlr8gEKzknugdTWAjg">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>r any accrued interest or penalties associated with unrecognized tax benefits during the&#160;years ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025. The Company believes that it has appropriate support for the income tax positions taken and to be taken on the Company&#8217;s tax returns and that the accruals for tax liabilities are adequate for all open&#160;years based on its assessment of many factors including past experience and interpretations of tax law applied to the facts of each matter. The Company&#8217;s federal and state income tax returns are open to audit under the statute of limitations for the fiscal&#160;years ended June&#160;30, 2022 through June&#160;30, 2025 for federal tax purposes and for the fiscal&#160;years ended June&#160;30,&#160;2021 through June&#160;30, 2025 for state tax purposes. To the extent the Company utilizes net operating losses (&#8220;NOLs&#8221;) generated in earlier&#160;years, such earlier&#160;years may also be subject to audit.</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_7_1_2025_To_6_30_2026_KseTYv8A0kKeZ3U92N1auA" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfComponentsOfIncomeTaxExpenseBenefitTableTextBlock" id="Tb_mpDvnrOaNkWBWYeT4ORJvg" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Income tax (expense) benefit for the&#160;years ended June&#160;30,&#160;2026 and 2025 is comprised of the following (in thousands):</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:80%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:60.72%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:3.1%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10